going to meet you What do you mean?

4
00:00:39,580 --> 00:00:45,260
What do you mean?

5
00:00:59,820 --> 00:01:02,620
Thank you.

6
00:01:35,040 --> 00:01:39,099
We were crossing yet another desert
when Kari got sick and collapsed.

7
00:01:39,300 --> 00:01:41,997
Tai kind of freaked out because it
seems that when they were younger,

8
00:01:42,080 --> 00:01:44,077
she almost died, and Tai blames himself.

9
00:01:44,160 --> 00:01:47,880
We soon discovered a deserted
city, and while Sora and T .K.

10
00:01:48,100 --> 00:01:51,394
watched over Kari, Tai and I
went in search of medicine.

11
00:01:51,600 --> 00:01:54,277
Machinedramon and his goons
were tracking our every move,

12
00:01:54,360 --> 00:01:58,277
and on our way back from the hospital,
we just barely escaped annihilation.

13
00:01:58,360 --> 00:02:00,477
When we finally rejoined the others,

14
00:02:00,560 --> 00:02:04,560
Machinedramon showed up and imploded
the building we were hiding in.

15
00:02:04,680 --> 00:02:06,197
Could things get any worse?

16
00:02:06,280 --> 00:02:07,110
Probably.

17
00:02:11,580 --> 00:02:12,620
Paraba! Umemon!

18
00:02:14,980 --> 00:02:18,057
How long do humans usually
sleep when they're sick, TK?

19
00:02:18,140 --> 00:02:19,757
It's tough to say for sure, Gatomon,

20
00:02:19,840 --> 00:02:22,277
but I guess anywhere between
eight hours and eight years,

21
00:02:22,360 --> 00:02:23,737
give or take a minute or so.

22
00:02:23,820 --> 00:02:27,297
Wow, then considering how high her
fever is, we'd better get comfortable.

23
00:02:27,380 --> 00:02:29,477
I wish one of the older kids were here.

24
00:02:29,560 --> 00:02:31,657
I bet they'd know how to wake her up.

25
00:02:31,740 --> 00:02:33,505
You'll think of something, TK.

26
00:02:36,200 --> 00:02:37,030
See?

27
00:02:37,113 --> 00:02:38,637
I knew you'd think of something.

28
00:02:38,720 --> 00:02:40,661
I'm still not sure that woke her.

29
00:02:43,160 --> 00:02:43,990
Huh?

30
00:02:44,160 --> 00:02:45,780
I could be wrong. Hi, Kari.

31
00:02:46,860 --> 00:02:49,440
Hit the snooze button one more time.

32
00:02:50,160 --> 00:02:50,990
Please.

33
00:02:51,073 --> 00:02:52,196
You've slept enough.

34
00:02:52,340 --> 00:02:53,281
How do you feel?

35
00:02:53,520 --> 00:02:55,060
I think my fever's gone.

36
00:02:55,380 --> 00:02:57,440
So, how long was I asleep for?

37
00:02:57,840 --> 00:02:59,737
Let's just say that when you fell asleep,

38
00:02:59,820 --> 00:03:02,517
I had nine lives, and now
I'm down to only three.

39
00:03:02,600 --> 00:03:03,718
Where is everybody?

40
